      "message": "requestUnbufferedDispatch(MotionEvent event) and requestImmediateDispatch() are very similar, except the AOSP requestUnbufferedDispatch is limited to touch events; \"Unbuffered\" has same meaning\"Immediate\" except the fields were added independently.   The naming of our added function could make clear the similarities and differences, like requestUnbufferedDispatchForAllInput()\n\nApart from the name, I am OK that the added function does not take a MotionEvent parameter and affects all input on the View after, because for button presses, each gamepad button DOWN event should have good latency; though I haven\u0027t verified that DOWN events are in fact buffered; I can check that.\n\n1 important usecase is gamepad button and analog stick latency for GFN/Gamestream.  For this usecase input should not be buffered until to VSYNC, because input is streamed to server.",
